<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Tesla returns two weeks after starting sertraline 50 mg each morning. He had mild nausea for four days and looser stools, now settled, and no headache, restlessness, or change in sleep. He has missed no doses. He has had his first session of exposure and response prevention and began building his list of feared situations. He still washes his hands about 50 times a day, but uses the ointment after each wash and the cracks are less painful. He has eaten two meals a day most days. He has had no suicidal thoughts. He saw Dr. Feinberg-Osei of psychiatry this morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medication tolerance</td><td>Mild nausea and loose stools for four days, now settled</td></tr><tr><td>Adherence</td><td>No missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Rituals</td><td>Washing about 50 times a day; counting and calculating unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>First ERP session; hierarchy started</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>Y-BOCS</td><td>27, down from 28</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

