    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Obsessive-compulsive disorder, severe (F42.2)</content>. Y-BOCS 27, down from 28 after two weeks, which is expected this early. Sertraline is well tolerated. Psychiatry confirms OCD with good insight and finds no tic disorder, bipolar disorder, psychosis, or obsessive-compulsive personality disorder. Suicide risk is low. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg; if the response is inadequate at six weeks, increase in 50 mg steps every four to six weeks as tolerated, as Dr. Feinberg-Osei advised.</item><item>Weekly ERP; homework from the hierarchy.</item><item>Collaborative safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Irritant hand dermatitis (L24.9)</content>. Improving with petrolatum. [S]<list><item>Continue petrolatum after each wash and cotton gloves at night.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Underweight from food rituals (R63.6)</content>. Weight steady at 63.9 kg. [S]<list><item>Dietitian visit next week; three fixed mealtimes.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Y-BOCS severity score (recorded in the note; no LOINC code found)</td><td>At baseline and about every 4 to 6 weeks during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>27, down from 28 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Comorbidity review: tics, bipolar disorder, psychosis, hoarding, body dysmorphic symptoms, and personality</td><td>At the initial assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Psychiatric interview today found none of these; depressive and anxiety symptoms are secondary to the OCD</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9 when given)</td><td>Every visit during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, or behavior since intake. Protective factors unchanged. Safety plan reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Sertraline adherence and adverse effects (nausea, diarrhea, sleep, activation, sexual effects)</td><td>Every visit and two weeks after each dose increase</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Early nausea and loose stools settled; no activation; no missed doses; dose unchanged at 50 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exposure and response prevention attendance and homework</td><td>Every visit during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First session done; hierarchy started</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI</td><td>Every visit while underweight</td><td>Completed today</td><td>63.9 kg, BMI 18.1, steady</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Hand skin</td><td>Every visit while dermatitis is present</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Fewer and shallower fissures</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Psychiatry consultation</td><td>For severe OCD at the start of treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today; diagnosis confirmed; titration plan agreed</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antipsychotic augmentation monitoring (weight, glucose, lipids, movement)</td><td>Only if an antipsychotic is added</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No augmentation; responding to sertraline and ERP</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Y-BOCS down by at least 35 percent (treatment response) by twenty-four weeks. In progress; target 2026-06-30 [S]</item><item>Rituals under one hour a day, with meals eaten without calculating. In progress; target 2026-06-30 [S]</item><item>BMI at least 18.5 with three meals a day. In progress; target 2026-06-30 [S]</item><item>Hands healed, with washing under 15 times a day. In progress; target 2026-04-07 [S]</item><item>At least six hours of sleep most nights. In progress; target 2026-06-30 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Patients With Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (2007); Guideline Watch: Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Patients With Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (2013); Obsessive-compulsive disorder and body dysmorphic disorder: treatment (CG31) (2005); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Review in four weeks, six weeks after starting sertraline. Next scheduled visit 2026-02-24: six-week OCD treatment review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
